# Fixed defect 2692, 2026-11-22, lane-crossing, a shape beside it: a record
# of another module holding a `(thread T)`, which belongs to the thread
# holding it as a C handle does, handed to `spawn`. Symptom: accepted.
# Cause: the record's fields were lowered only once the declarations' walk
# reached its module, after the root's `main` (spec § 11).
use crew

function body(c: crew.Crew) -> i64
    return c.n

function main()
    t = spawn(body, crew.made()).must()  #~ thread_crossing
    print(t.wait())
